# Scacelith - Magyar
# Translation of assets/i18n/en.lang (same keys, same {n}). Plurals: one|other; a Hungarian noun
# stays singular after a number, so both forms are usually the same words ("1 lépés", "5 lépés").
# Register: formal address, as Microsoft and Apple Hungarian do ("Válassza ki...", "Ön" only where a
# pronoun is needed); buttons and menu entries are nouns or verbal nouns ("Új játszma", "Kilépés").
# Titles in capitals with their accents (ÚJ JÁTSZMA). Terms follow the Hungarian glossary: világos /
# sötét (lowercase inside a sentence), értékszám and "Élő" for Elo, játékidő for time control,
# "fogott bábu" for touch-move, "mp" for seconds.
# No case suffix and no article a/az is attached to a placeholder: their form depends on how the value
# sounds, so the sentences put a name, a number or a square in the nominative or after a colon.

